my name is Stephanie Vina I'm a  professor at Q tech TU delft and I'm  working with a team of people from  physics and computer science in order to  build a quantum Internet  a quantum Internet fundamentally  enhances the internet technology that we  have today it enables us to send quantum  bits qubits from one point on the  Internet to another and by doing this we  can implement applications that are  impossible on the internet that we have  today  a quantum Internet has many applications  and one application that I'm quite  excited about is secure quantum  computing in the cloud on my quantum  internet you could use a very simple  quantum device a quantum terminal to  perform a computation on a remote  quantum computer in such a way that the  quantum computer cannot learn what  computation you're performing this is  interesting for example to perform a  simulation on this quantum computer of a  preparatory new material this way you  can perform that simulation that's no  classical computer might be able to do  in such a way that you don't have to  give away your material design  so we are building a quantum network in  the Netherlands which might become a  world's first in which we connect  quantum processors small quantum  computers in different cities the first  link will be built between our location  here in Delft and a place in The Hague  with a Dutch telecom we then want to  expand this network to other cities and  also want to make it available to you in  a few years from now
 

